{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent","id":655909,"title":"Demonic Exigent","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-07T20:36:45-07:00","id":655909,"title":"Demonic Exigent","content":"So if I recall correctly, it's been established already that only gods can muck around with Exigence, but does it break anything if I wanted, say, a chosen of Ligier without any of the other baggage that comes from being an Infernal? Or what about the story possibilities that come from a first age twilight who got his hands on a handful of black market exigencies and decided to do SCIENCE to them?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5257-queshire","name":"Queshire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:43:19-07:00","id":655947,"title":"","content":"Giving demons access to the Exigence undermines the very concept of the Exigence, but you can just give them access to Akuma who work like Exigents.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:43:29-07:00","id":655950,"title":"","content":"Maybe Ligier just made something similar. Doesn't necessarily have to be an Exigent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T20:53:03-07:00","id":655957,"title":"","content":"Nothing breaks, I've asked this question in the RPG.net thread before and the basic response was &quot;it's not canonically possible, but if you want to make it happen then go for it I guess&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-07T22:00:08-07:00","id":656053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tiresias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=655947#post655947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving demons access to the Exigence undermines the very concept of the Exigence, but you can just give them access to Akuma who work like Exigents.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've pretty much universally been bored with the canonical Akuma thing, so pretty much the first thing that jumped to mind after hearing about Exigence not being accessible by demons was that I'd just make Akuma demonic Exigents. Opens a lot of doors and doesn't really get rid of anything I particularly cared for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1817-opmegs","name":"OpMegs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1817_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T01:05:36-07:00","id":656202,"title":"","content":"Not all new Exalted need be Exigents, even if we'll be able to use the Exigents stuff to make any Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T03:21:23-07:00","id":656306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=656202#post656202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all new Exalted need be Exigents, even if we'll be able to use the Exigents stuff to make any Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div> Yeah, if you want to use the Exigent rules to create some sort of &quot;Daemonaic&quot;, go for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:05:26-07:00","id":656389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent#post655909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or what about the story possibilities that come from a first age twilight who got his hands on a handful of black market exigencies and decided to do SCIENCE to them?</div> </div> </div> </div>If this results in &quot;the Twilight Exalts people himself,&quot; personally I think it screws a little too much with what it means to be Exalted vs what it means to be a god.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:42:23-07:00","id":656404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=655950#post655950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe Ligier just made something similar. Doesn't necessarily have to be an Exigent.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I recall, there was a post a while back mentioning that some Yozi tried to create their own exalts but were <i>disquieted</i> by the result. That particular word struck me as leaving open the possibility that they <i>succeeded </i>in ways they did not like. Whether the price was too high, or there was <i>something </i>about the exalt that made them uneasy.<br /> <br /> So they could still be running around.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T05:46:15-07:00","id":656406,"title":"","content":"Exalted has lots of players of similiar, high, power level, so I don't think it's going to break anything to take the crunch from Exigents and apply it to build something else entirely. But redefining the Exigence to be able to be used by someone else than gods probably results in some wear and tear down the line when plot hooks don't take this into account.<br /> <br /> Besides that, crunch-wise, I'm pretty sure Exigents are written for precisely that - people asking &quot;what if I want to make X?&quot; - it supposedly gives great guidelines for hacking together custom charmsets, so if that works, you'll be set.<br /> <br /> And Ligier has tons of awesome themes to explore, so as a side note, I totally encourage you to do this, and then share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T11:11:39-07:00","id":656760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Queshire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent#post655909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So if I recall correctly, it's been established already that only gods can muck around with Exigence, but does it break anything if I wanted, say, a chosen of Ligier without any of the other baggage that comes from being an Infernal? Or what about the story possibilities that come from a first age twilight who got his hands on a handful of black market exigencies and decided to do SCIENCE to them?<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Exigency derives from the Unconquered Sun, and it's flat out impossible for demons to create Exigents. I think it's impossible for elementals to create Exigents as well, at least I haven't seen anything suggesting they can. Exigents are specifically something that gods create through the assistance of the Unconquered Sun.<br /> <br /> That said, it sounds entirely reasonable for demons to have discovering some way of improving or bestowing power on mortals. In fact, with Akuma going away as a thing, I think this could be a very reasonable way of replacing/redefining the original Akuma concept.<br /> <br /> Just say, a demon can have exactly one Akuma servant, and it bestows a lot of its power on him. This weakens the demon quite a bit, and more importantly causes some kind of drawback to the demon's Yozi (maybe it gets a -1 on all rolls for every Akuma that serves one of its souls). This creates a &quot;soft cap&quot; in how many Akuma you can have running around. So that way you can have cool antagonists with powersets based off of neato demons, while at the same time not running into the problem that Akuma had in 2nd edition (which was a theoretically unlimited number of them running around with Yozi charms).<br /> <br /> I imagine that, even if these guys weren't actual Exigents, the Exigent rule set would still be a wonderful base for creating them and building/balancing their charmsets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T12:35:40-07:00","id":656806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=656760#post656760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the problem that Akuma had in 2nd edition (which was a theoretically unlimited number of them running around with Yozi charms).</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never felt this was a problem (aside from what I've seen on the forum about how Return of the Scarlet Empress handled them.) Their numbers are limited by the number of Exalted who exist and are willing and able to give themselves to a Third Circle demon -- not something easy even if you want to do it! They don't generally live any longer than regular Exalted, either. I figure they might be more numerous than Lunars, but there are probably at most a couple thousand at any one time, and probably far fewer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:18:46-07:00","id":656847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=656806#post656806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never felt this was a problem (aside from what I've seen on the forum about how Return of the Scarlet Empress handled them.) Their numbers are limited by the number of Exalted who exist and are willing and able to give themselves to a Third Circle demon -- not something easy even if you want to do it! They don't generally live any longer than regular Exalted, either. I figure they might be more numerous than Lunars, but there are probably at most a couple thousand at any one time, and probably far fewer.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Raia in The Akuma Who Loved Me encountered Lucien and &quot;brought her life at the cost of her soul&quot; which is a pact in the same way that a mugging is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T13:18:57-07:00","id":656848,"title":"","content":"Except the rules allow for mortals and God-Blooded and other things to become Akuma.<br /> <br /> Also, re: Elemental Exigents, this is something I specifically asked about; no, they can't work the Exigence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:32:56-07:00","id":657026,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=656806#post656806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never felt this was a problem (aside from what I've seen on the forum about how Return of the Scarlet Empress handled them.) Their numbers are limited by the number of Exalted who exist and are willing and able to give themselves to a Third Circle demon -- not something easy even if you want to do it! They don't generally live any longer than regular Exalted, either. I figure they might be more numerous than Lunars, but there are probably at most a couple thousand at any one time, and probably far fewer.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem was with mortals being Akuma. The Yozi could take a mortal and turn them into one of their Akuma - and keep in mind that mortal-Akuma being slightly more powerful than a Dragon Blooded (they had the same Essence pool but were using Solar-tier Charms). There was also no limit to how many could be made - the Yozi could empower one-million mortals as Akuma and crush any force in Creation that tried to face them. <br /> <br /> The Akuma rules were horrible, and at the time Neph and Holden were both clear that the rules were garbage.<br /> <br /> Now, all that said, the idea of mortals gaining power from demons by selling their souls is very cool and thematic, but the mechanics of doing so in 2nd edition were terrible. This idea though is probably worth exploring in some form, though ensuring that there is some kind of a &quot;cap&quot; on how many Akuma there can be, and probably creating their own custom powers (likely determined by what sort of pact they have formed and what demon they have formed it with).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T15:49:49-07:00","id":657062,"title":"","content":"Mortal akuma have access to Yozi charms and Dragon-Blooded essence pools?! I thought they were just endowed Demon-Bloods... ('cuz that's all they were in the 1E Player's Guide.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:00:53-07:00","id":657077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=657062#post657062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mortal akuma have access to Yozi charms and Dragon-Blooded essence pools?! I thought they were just endowed Demon-Bloods... ('cuz that's all they were in the 1E Player's Guide.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much in 2e. Yozi Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:03:47-07:00","id":657097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=657026#post657026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, all that said, the idea of mortals gaining power from demons <b>by selling their souls</b> is very cool and thematic\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it? Moreover, is it something that has a place in Exalted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:11:50-07:00","id":657125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=657097#post657097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? Moreover, is it something that has a place in Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Metaphorically, at least, why not? The 2e GSP Exaltation was a Faustian deal, a metaphorical selling of the soul.<br /> <br /> It's pretty much ok as long as it's not literal, unless literally selling your soul turns you into some terrible realm-stepping ghost-exalt monster, which would be a pretty cool splat maybe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T16:42:32-07:00","id":657143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/655909-demonic-exigent?p=657097#post657097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? Moreover, is it something that has a place in Exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>By &quot;selling ones soul&quot; I was terming it in slightly more metaphorical as selling ones services in exchange for power, though pledging yourself and your literal soul to the enemies of Creation in change for power is something that has been around since Abyssals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T17:15:02-07:00","id":657162,"title":"","content":"Given that certain kinds of financial exchange are basically the default interaction between humans and demons, whether it be dreams in exchange for the wonders of Makarios or getting yourself turned into some useful, immortal thing by Alveua, or Ligier just kind of giving you something because he's cool like that, I have an inclination to look elsewhere for a diverse array of Infernal Exalted. That and how the portrayal in the past has always felt a bit confused to me; I mean, is being an akuma what you get in <i>exchange</i> for your soul, or is it a marker of being owned by a Yozi that they get in exchange for doing something else for you? Certainly, akuma powers have hardly ever felt worth the price of admission in any case where the motivation was something other than dedication to the Yozis. But yeah, other creatures as Exalted following the basic premise of all of the rest; to be Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-08T18:16:11-07:00","id":657244,"title":"","content":"I had an idea for someone being empowered by Alveua by having a prosthetic that\u2019s made from the willing sacrifice of someone with whom they share an extremely powerful bond, resulting in something that\u2019s greater than a Mortal enhanced by a hellforged artifact. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}